    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="6f2e568f-e5b2-5001-b65d-7ed8732f9377" activityNameId="d313a4ec-de78-5aac-9453-db77d63dc51b" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">xxx Hardwood, standing, under bark, in forest</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: xxx Hardwood, standing, under bark, in forest
The volume does not include the bark. CO2 assimilation is based on 49.4% carbon in the wood including the bark (12%). Biomass energy equals gross calorific value including bark.;
Synonyms: Beech, Buche; 
UUID: eda3df4e-84d5-327c-a694-0b0d78facc62
Includes the CO2 absorption from air and the land use for the trees to grow. Forest road area is not included in the land use
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Natural growth. Relates to the forest area and CO2 from air needed to produce beech. It is assumed, that other hardwood species need similar time and area to grow.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: Literature 
Extrapolations: see Geography and Technology
Uncertainty adjustments: The assumptions that different species are growing at the same rate as beech and that Germany is representative for central Europe are considered in the uncertainties.
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_eda3df4e-84d5-327c-a694-0b0d78facc62.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="20a9bf48-6cea-59b4-ad08-000cb981f2d0" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
